# Temporary workaround: GKD Pixel2 enters "mem" (deep) suspend correctly
# but never wakes from it (see the KNOWN ONGOING ISSUE comment on the
# rk817 node in rk3326s-gkd-pixel2.dts) - firmware alone decides what
# wakes the CPU cores once they're powered off for a sleep mode this
# deep, and two separate attempts at fixing that (a dev_pm_set_wake_irq()
# kernel patch, and a ported rockchip_pm_config.c sending the correct
# wakeup-config to firmware via SIP_SUSPEND_MODE) were both tested on
# real hardware with no change in behavior. Until the real root cause is
# found, default to "freeze" (s2idle) instead: CPU cores stay mostly on
# and idle rather than powering off, so a normal GPIO IRQ (e.g. the power
# button) can wake the system the ordinary way, without depending on
# whatever firmware-level wake-source arming "mem" needs and isn't
# getting. Same mechanism RK3576 uses for the same class of issue.

. /etc/profile.d/001-functions

MYSLEEPMODE=$(get_setting system.suspendmode)
if [ -z "${MYSLEEPMODE}" ]
then
  /usr/bin/suspendmode freeze
fi
